# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings
#
# This repo is edited from at least two places - a Windows VDI (CRLF) and tooling
# that writes LF - which made git report whole files as rewritten when only the
# line endings differed. A 1,533-insertion / 1,533-deletion diff on an unchanged
# file makes review impossible and buries real changes.
#
# text=auto normalises text files to LF in the repository and checks them out with
# the platform's native endings, so both editors stay happy and diffs stay honest.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that must keep a specific ending regardless of platform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.sh   text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evidence - never normalise
#
# The sha256 of every input export is recorded in export-manifest.json, cited by
# the workbook's Evidence sheet, and re-checked by publish_month.py immediately
# before upload. Any rewrite of line endings changes those bytes and therefore the
# hash, which would break the evidence chain and block publication.
#
# Cycle data is gitignored today (*/input/, */output/), so this is defence in
# depth against a future force-add rather than a live problem. Deliberate, because
# a corrupted hash would surface as a confusing publication failure months later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv   -text
*.xlsx  -text
*.xlsm  -text
*.docx  -text
*.dotx  -text
*.pdf   -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary / credential material - never diffed, never normalised
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem   -text
*.pfx   -text
*.cer   -text
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diff hints
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.py    diff=python
*.md    diff=markdown
